# Support — ShieldTracker DeFi

**Email:** support@shieldtrackerdefi.com
**Replies:** within 2 business days

Write to support@shieldtrackerdefi.com with what you were trying to do and what happened instead. There is no account, no login, and no ticket number — just send the mail.

---

## 1. Before you write

Most problems come down to one of the answers below. Worth a look first — it will usually be faster than waiting for a reply.

<details>
<summary><b>The results show a dash instead of numbers</b></summary>

All three main fields need a value: buy price, sell price, and amount held. Leave any of them empty and there is nothing to calculate. Fees are optional and default to zero.

</details>

<details>
<summary><b>The profit looks wrong</b></summary>

Buy price and sell price are per unit, not totals. If you bought 0.5 BTC at $30,000 each, the buy price is `30000` and the amount held is `0.5` — not `15000`. Fees are entered as percentages, so `0.1` means 0.1%, not 10%.

</details>

<details>
<summary><b>The extension is in the wrong language</b></summary>

It follows your browser's display language and is available in English and Swedish. If your browser is set to another language, you will see the notice screen with a button that opens the page in English. To change your browser language, go to Chrome settings, then Languages, and move your preferred language to the top.

</details>

<details>
<summary><b>Does it fetch live crypto prices?</b></summary>

No. It never connects to the network. You supply both prices yourself, which is also why it works offline and why it collects nothing about you. See the [privacy policy](PRIVACY.md).

</details>

<details>
<summary><b>Where is my data stored?</b></summary>

On your own computer, in your browser's local extension storage, if it is stored at all. Nothing is uploaded, and removing the extension removes everything it kept.

</details>

<details>
<summary><b>Can I use it for stocks or other assets?</b></summary>

Yes. The maths is the same for anything you buy at one price and sell at another. The labels say dollars, but the numbers are unitless — use any currency, as long as you use the same one in every field.

</details>

<details>
<summary><b>How do I remove it?</b></summary>

Right-click the extension icon in the Chrome toolbar and choose **Remove from Chrome**. Or open `chrome://extensions`, find ShieldTracker DeFi, and select **Remove**. Its local storage goes with it.

</details>

## 2. Reporting a bug

Include these and the fix usually takes one round instead of three:

1. The exact numbers you entered in each field.
2. The result you saw, and the result you expected.
3. Your Chrome version, from `chrome://version`.
4. Your operating system, and a screenshot if you have one.

## 3. Requesting a feature

Suggestions are welcome, especially for currencies, additional fee models, or languages. Send them to the same address. The extension deliberately stays a local calculator, so anything that requires fetching data from the internet is out of scope by design.

## 4. What this extension is not

> ShieldTracker DeFi is not financial, investment, or tax advice, and it is not a wallet, an exchange, or a portfolio service. It never asks for a seed phrase, a private key, an exchange API key, or a password — if anything ever appears to ask you for one in its name, it is not us. Do not send credentials of any kind by email.

